  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Angoroside-C and the High-affinity choline transporter, mediated through Caspase-5. Angoroside-C is identified as a target of Caspase-5, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and a complex acetate derivative. These compounds all ultimately target the High-affinity choline transporter, indicating a pathway where Angoroside-C may influence the transporter through Caspase-5. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying levels of support from different compounds. The evidence highlights a possible mechanism involving Caspase-5 as a bridge between Angoroside-C and the choline transporter, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same pathway supports the hypothesis, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Angoroside-C in this process.",
